    "issue_body_preview": "### Issue Summary\r\n\r\nSometimes internal server errors occur and the next server will respond with a `serverError: \"Something went wrong while executing the operation.\"` (but still status code 200). Because of status 200 the frontend will not recognize it as an error and will still show a success toast (although something went wrong).\r\nFormbricks should check the responses for a serverError when accessing backend functions:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (result?.serverError) {\r\n    throw new Error(\"Something went wrong\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Use eg #3301 to trigger an unsuccessful server only action\r\n2. success toast will pop up although the operation actually failed\r\n\r\nThis happens in many places where the toast will pop up when there is no error during a server side action.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nAn error toast indicating the issue pops up (instead of falsely suggesting a successful operation)\r\n\r\n### Other information\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n\r\n- [X] Formbricks Cloud (app.formbricks.com)\r\n- [ ] Self-hosted Formbricks\r\n\r\n### Desktop (please complete the following information)\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n- all Browsers\r\n```\r\n",
